%description:
Tests TcpSocket::setSynRetries() on an open socket, the Linux socket option
TCP_SYNCNT after connect(). Linux reads TCP_SYNCNT at each timeout, so the
value acts from the next retransmission on. The client connects at t=0 with
the synRetries parameter of the module (12), and at t=0.5 s, in SYN_SENT, it
sets one SYN retry. The tester removes each SYN: the client sends its SYN again
at t=1 and fails at the next timeout, at t=3. Before the repair, the value
reached only the open command of the next connect(), and the client went on
with 12 retries (the packetdrill scripts nonblocking-sendto-errnos and
nonblocking-connect-bypass-errno of inet-gpl).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 10s
*.cli_tcp.initialRto = 1s
*.cli_app.synRetriesScript="0.5 1"  # TCP_SYNCNT 1, in SYN_SENT
*.tcptester.script="a1 delete; a2 delete; a3 delete; a4 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
[1.001 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> CLOSED  (on TIMEOUT_CONN_ESTAB)
[10.000] tcpdump finished, A:2 B:0 segments
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
